#: ../../chapter03.rst:594
msgid "3.3.5 Settings Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:595
msgid "Server Agent administrators can customize and configure many settings at the Server Console level by modifying the contents of the Settings Manager section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:597
msgid "From here you can also access the **\"Offline Folders\"** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:602
msgid "This section lists all the cloud folders which have been enabled for **\"Offline Access\"**, meaning users who have access to offline folders can access and edit the contents of such folders even when they are not online. All the changes done to files in offline folders will be automatically synced as soon as the users come back online."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:607
msgid "OFFLINE FOLDERS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:609
msgid "**\"Add New Offline Folder\"** You can click this link to configure a folder as an Offline Folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:612
msgid "Settings Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:615
msgid "Bandwidth Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:617
msgid "As an administrator you have full control over how much bandwidth should be consumed for uploading contents to the cloud and also for downloading contents from the cloud. You can also control how many consequent uploads and downloads are allowed at any one time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:622
msgid "SETTINGS MANAGER - BANDWIDTH CONTROL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:624
msgid "**\"Download Bandwidth Limit (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)\"** Default is **\"0\"**. This setting is applied to the local machine (Server Agent). Usually something > 100KB/s is good. If it is too small, it can negatively affect performance and usability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:626
msgid "**\"Upload Bandwidth Limit (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)\"** Default is **\"0\"**. This setting is applied to the local machine (Server Agent). Usually something > 100KB/s is good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:628
msgid "**\"Number of Upload/Download Threads\"** Default is **\"5\"**. Set this from 5-10 in general. In some case, if you set it to a very big number such as 20, it may negatively affect performance. For example, if you are using Amazon S3 and Amazon S3 or other Cloud services may have per-client thread policy so if you have too many concurrent upload/download, it may get regulated outside of the Server Agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:631
msgid "Cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:636
msgid "SETTINGS MANAGER - CACHE SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:638
msgid "You can change the location of Cache (for files downloaded locally from cloud). You can also set the cache size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:643
msgid "Sync Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:648
msgid "SETTINGS MANAGER - SYNC CONTROL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:650
msgid "**\"Throttle Sync\"** Default is **\"False\"**. If you set this flag to **\"True\"** it will stop and start the sync depending on the available bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:652
msgid "**\"Sync Throttled Upload Bandwidth (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)\"** Default is **\"0\"**. Where **\"0\"** means unlimited bandwidth is available for upload sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:654
msgid "**\"Sync Throttled Download Bandwidth (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)\"** Default is **\"0\"**. Where **\"0\"** means unlimited bandwidth is available for download sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:656
msgid "**\"Full Speed Sync Stop Hour (dafault 7:00)\"** Default is **\"7\"**. Use this setting to set when full sync stops, to prevent bogging down your system during business hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:658
msgid "**\"Full Speed Sync Start Hour (dafault 20:00)\"** Default is **\"20\"**.  Use this setting to set when full sync starts, to prevent bogging down your system during business hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:660
msgid "**\"Scan local files and sync up to cloud as necessary\"** Default is **\"False\"**. Set this to **\"True\"** if you want the agent to scan the local file system and make sure that everything which is not synced to the cloud is truly synced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:662
msgid "**\"Scan cloud files and sync up to local as necessary\"** Default is **\"False\"**. Set this to **\"True\"** if you want the agent to scan the cloud and make sure that everything which is not synced to the local file system is truly synced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:664
msgid "**\"Optimize Sync Down Notification\"** Default is **\"False\"**. If you want to see sync down notifications, then set this to **\"True\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:666
msgid "**\"Ignore file dummy change notification\"** Default is **\"False\"**. If you don't want to see dummy file change notifications, then set this to **\"True\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:668
msgid "**\"Enable sync folder permission in attached folder\"** Default is **\"False\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:672
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:674
msgid "Administrator can locate the cache directory under **\"Advanced\"** option in settings. Using the **\"Cache Size Limit (MB)\"** field can specify the size limit for the cache file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:680
msgid "SETTINGS MANAGER - ADVANCED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:682
msgid "**\"Do not Mount Drive\"** Default is **\"False\"**. When you set this to **\"True\"** local drive on the Server Agent is unmounted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:684
msgid "**\"Domain Controller IP or Hostname\"** This setting is empty by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:686
msgid "**\"Enable In-place Open Zip File\"** Default is **\"False\"**. This field enables in-place editing on files which are in zipped folders in the cloud. You can also specify the maximum size for zipped files that are allowed for In-place editing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:688
msgid "**\"Max Size of Zip File Allowed to Open Inplace\"** This is **\"20\"** by default. Use this field to set the maximum size of Zip Files that can be opened inside the Cloud Drive in MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:690
msgid "**\"Ignore Settings in Group Policy\"** Default is **\"False\"**. When you set this flag to **\"True\"**, the configured settings in the Web Portal will be ignored and the settings configured here under ``Settings`` > ``Advanced`` will take precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:692
msgid "**\"Interval to Keep Group Relationship in Cache (Min)\"** The default is **\"60\"** minutes. This field is a performance optimization setting. The Server Agent will check the remote requests against the ACL (Access Control) set on the local files. Most of the times it involves Active Directory or NT domain group membership checking. The group membership checking is a CPU intensive work so the result is cached to improve performance. This controls how long the result will be cached. If users are not changing group frequently, you can set the interval to a long period of time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:694
msgid "**\"Purge File Sys DB Upon Start\"** The default is **\"False\"**. If you change this setting to True, upon startup the client will purge the cached cloud storage state file. This allows the client to rebuild the database as if it is being started for the first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:696
msgid "**\"Upload Hidden Files\"** The default is **\"False\"**. If this flag is set to **\"True\"** then hidden files will also be uploaded to the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:698
msgid "**\"Upload System Files\"** The default is **\"False\"**. If this flag when set to **\"True\"** then system files will also be uploaded to the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:701
msgid "Trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:703
msgid "The audit trace log can grow exponentially if not kept under control. As an administrator you can specify the number of days to keep the audit trace. **\"Days of Audit Trace to Keep\"** setting is the field to specify the duration to keep the trace for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:705
msgid "Trace Level when set to **\"0\"** which is the default does not collect any traces meaning it is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:707
msgid "Trace Level 1 – error will collect all the error traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:709
msgid "Trace Level 2 – warning will collect warning traces along with errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:711
msgid "Trace Level 3 – info will collect errors, warnings, as well as info traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:713
msgid "Trace Level 100 – verbose helps developers to collect detailed traces which helps them when debugging issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:716
msgid "When it is necessary to collect DebugView trace for debugging purpose, the Trace Level typically is set to 101."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter03.rst:721
msgid "SETTINGS MANAGER - TRACE"
msgstr ""
